# nat.suite — two nodes meet on a LAN, then both move behind NAT and the
# swarm re-forms by hole-punching.
#
# Every step is built from nothing in one simulation, as in tor.suite. The two
# transport tests live in separate suites because each mutates two-nodes and
# nothing puts it back: tor-link's leave-lan downs node2's LAN interface, and
# nat-punch's enter-nat then finds none to move behind NAT.
bootstrap-user-software-key
adopt-node
nat-punch
